      "text": "**If you mean Jurong, Singapore: I’d exercise indoors right now.** At **4:00 pm on Saturday, October 17**, the latest West-region reading I could find was **221 µg/m³ for 1-hour PM2.5**, in the **High** band. Singapore’s health guidance says healthy people should **avoid strenuous outdoor exercise** at that level; children, pregnant people, older adults, and people with heart or lung conditions should **avoid outdoor activity** for the next hour. ([haze.sg](https://www.haze.sg/))\n\nA brief, easy walk may be reasonable if you’re healthy and feel well, but skip the run or workout. **Check the West-region 1-hour PM2.5 reading on haze.gov.sg or myENV again before going out**—haze levels can change. It’s also about **31°C (87°F)**, so take care with the heat. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))",
